#### Accordions for collapsible content
<AccordionGroup>
<Accordion title="Troubleshooting authentication issues">
  - **401 Unauthorized**: Check that your API key is valid and not expired
  - **403 Forbidden**: Ensure your account has the required permissions
  - **Rate limited**: Implement exponential backoff for retries
</Accordion>

<Accordion title="Common error codes">
  - `INVALID_PAN`: The PAN format is incorrect
  - `INVALID_GSTIN`: The GSTIN format is incorrect
  - `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE`: The upstream service is temporarily unavailable
</Accordion>
</AccordionGroup>

### API documentation components

#### Parameter fields
<ParamField path="pan" type="string" required>
PAN (Permanent Account Number) to verify. Must be a valid 10-character alphanumeric code.
</ParamField>

<ParamField body="gstin" type="string" required>
GSTIN (GST Identification Number) to search. Must be a valid 15-character code.
</ParamField>

<ParamField query="page" type="integer" default="1">
Page number for pagination. Range: 1-1000.
</ParamField>

<ParamField header="Authorization" type="string" required>
Bearer token for API authentication. Format: `Bearer YOUR_API_KEY`
</ParamField>

#### Response fields
<ResponseField name="code" type="integer" required>
HTTP status code indicating the result of the request.
</ResponseField>

<ResponseField name="data" type="object">
Response data containing the verification or search results.
</ResponseField>

<ResponseField name="message" type="string">
Human-readable message describing the result or error.
</ResponseField>

#### Expandable nested fields
<ResponseField name="data" type="object">
Complete response object with all verification details.

<Expandable title="Data properties">
  <ResponseField name="status" type="string">
  Verification status: "valid", "invalid", or "pending".
  </ResponseField>

  <ResponseField name="details" type="object">
  Additional details about the verification result.

  <Expandable title="Details">
    <ResponseField name="name" type="string">
    Name associated with the verified identifier.
    </ResponseField>

    <ResponseField name="verification_date" type="string">
    ISO 8601 formatted timestamp of verification.
    </ResponseField>
  </Expandable>
  </ResponseField>
</Expandable>
</ResponseField>

